meta {
  name: 07 ⚡ Applicant submits offer (FIRES KAFKA)
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{host}}/api/offers
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{applicant_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "listingId": {{canary_listing_id}},
    "amount": 900000,
    "currency": "NGN",
    "message": "Kafka canary offer — ignore. If you see this, the canary worked."
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
}

docs {
  **This is the trigger.** Submitting the offer:
    1. Writes the offer row.
    2. Writes an `outbox_events` row in the SAME transaction (atomic).
    3. The `OutboxRelay` background poll picks it up and publishes to the
       `offer.submitted.v1` Kafka topic.
    4. The `OfferSubmittedListener` consumer in this same app reads the
       event and writes a notification row for the listing owner.

  A 201 here only proves the synchronous half (offer + outbox row). The
  notification check in step 09 is what proves Kafka is actually wired.
}
